## Symptom

Doctor/state freshness is a fixed 120s window (relay_doctor.ml:285-291) while the connector self-scales with observed pass work (B291). On a many-root host a healthy root last_ok ages approximately one full pass period (live measured on xsm: 4-6 min passes), so connector_check and Relay_state.derive_health can classify a healthy connector as stale/wedged and recommend starting another, and the B294 register guard fresh arm misfires (pid-alive usually saves it; roots with older state files lose that arm).

## Fix direction

Scale the doctor window from recorded pass metadata or a C2C_RELAY_DOCTOR_FRESHNESS_S override; treat recorded-pid liveness as sufficient evidence in connector_owns_alias.

## Evidence

CLI review 2026-09-17 + live audit (pass timings 4m08s and 5m31s observed on xsm).